comments[4]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-12T02:01:13.150Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 7 is the final fix round for #233. This single follow-up consolidates additional review observations, as requested by the orchestrator; it does not assert that every observation reproduces after the round-7 changes. Validate each against the final head, deduplicate covered cases, and retain real SDK must-refuse/must-allow tests plus behavioral revert evidence for any fix.\n\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBR](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876674): Report import conflicts on the workflow path that produces no tracker diff.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBZ](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876686): Validate ambiguous legacy number-only ownership before closeout.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBc](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876691): Recover exclusive leases safely when publication succeeds but directory flush fails.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBe](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876695): Require an actual matching reference tag before planning tag detachment.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBi](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876701): Reconcile contradictory external_ref claims at the import write boundary.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBo](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876710): Check partial legacy link markers against an existing repository field.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auBu](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876718): Avoid retaining an ownership-refused plan when no SDK journal exists.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB1](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876728): Scope retained recovery plans to selected refresh IDs without dropping fresh updates.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB7](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876736): Handle contradictory identities in blocker self-exclusion; dependency indexing is addressed in round 7.\n- [PRRT_kwDOTbN4pM62auB_](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/pull/233#discussion_r4544876746): Use canonical lowercase reference tags in the citation-adoption fixture.\n\nExplicit identity-conflict isolation in closeout and real-tracker dry-run fixtures are already addressed by round 7. Existing curated-reopen, Projects and search follow-ups keep their separate scope. Do not delete append-only tracker evidence or reply to/resolve review threads while implementing this follow-up.\n\nPM: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/blob/main/.agents/pm/issues/pm-github-reference-identity-followup.toon"
  "2026-11-12T08:46:16.856Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 9 corrects this record only: removed the auxiliary gh reference to PR 233 so its identity agrees with issue 236. The PR is retained as a docs link. Existing history and the deferred implementation scope are unchanged."
  "2026-11-12T10:16:19.276Z",codex-github230-1111,"The priority dependency-index ambiguity from issue 236 is addressed in PR 233 round 10: a second claimant through external_ref is included by shared githubOwnershipClaims, reports ambiguous_github_dependency_owner, and writes no edge. Regression coverage uses real SDK trackers and also checks endpoint ownership under the native mutation lock. Other deferred observations retain their existing scope."
  "2026-11-12T17:35:01.802Z",codex-github230-1111,"Round 13 optional duplication check found a pre-existing five-line exact clone in projects.ts:630-634 and 699-701, in Project ownership-index setup. projects.ts has identical blob 71df0c3606f90feaeb53e1db6d415c57285d3530 at orchestrator base 5f6749f and in this round; no Project production logic was changed. npm run duplication reports one 53-token clone at the unchanged zero threshold. Preserve the selected-item-only scoped pull behavior when consolidating this setup. Deferred here rather than expanding the three requested fixes; required round-13 tests and checks are green."
